Below is a practical, step‑by‑step playbook you can follow (or adapt) to build a modern, production‑ready front‑end for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole journey – from planning & design to code, testing, and deployment – and sprinkle in concrete examples, best‑practice tips, and tool recommendations.

---

## 1️⃣ Planning & Design

| Step | What to do | Why it matters |
|------|------------|----------------|
| **Define goals & KPIs** | Identify conversion targets, average order value, bounce rate, etc. | Keeps the team focused on business outcomes. |
| **Create personas** | Build realistic buyer profiles. | Guides UX decisions. |
| **Sketch wireframes** | Rough layout of key pages (home, category, product, cart, checkout). | Early validation of flow. |
| **Prototype in Figma / Sketch** | Interactive mock‑ups, clickable flows. | Hand‑off to dev with fewer surprises. |
| **Accessibility audit** | Check color contrast, keyboard navigation, ARIA roles. | Improves usability & SEO. |
| **SEO & performance checklist** | Structured data, meta tags, image sizes, lazy loading. | Faster pages rank higher. |

> **Tip:** Keep a shared “Design System” file (components, colors, typography) so designers and developers stay in sync.

---

## 2️⃣ Choose Your Tech Stack

| Layer | Options | Recommendation |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular, Svelte | **React + Next.js** (SSR + SSG + ISR) |
| **State mgmt** | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Recoil, Context API | **Redux Toolkit** (for complex global state) |
| **Styling** | CSS Modules, Styled‑Components, Emotion, Tailwind CSS | **Tailwind CSS** (utility‑first, fast prototyping) |
| **Component library** | Material‑UI, Ant Design, Chakra UI, Headless UI | **Chakra UI** (accessibility out‑of‑the‑box) |
| **Type system** | JavaScript, TypeScript | **TypeScript** (runtime safety) |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library, Cypress | **Jest + RTL** for unit, **Cypress** for E2E |
| **Build & deploy** | Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, AWS Amplify | **Vercel** (Next.js integration) |
| **Analytics** | Google Analytics, Plausible, Segment | **Google Analytics 4** + **Segment** for unified tracking |
| **Payment** | Stripe, PayPal, Braintree | **Stripe** (modern API, strong docs) |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> * Server‑side rendering → instant first paint & SEO.  
> * Static generation for product pages → lightning‑fast.  
> * Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR) → keep pages fresh without rebuilds.

---

## 3️⃣ Project Skeleton

```bash
my-ecommerce/
├─ public/
│  ├─ images/
│  └─ favicon.ico
├─ src/
│  ├─ components/
│  │  ├─ ui/          # Button, Input, Modal, etc.
│  │  ├─ layout/      # Header, Footer, Sidebar
│  │  └─ pages/       # ProductCard, CartItem, etc.
│  ├─ hooks/
│  ├─ store/          # Redux slices
│  ├─ pages/          # Next.js pages (index.tsx, [slug].tsx)
│  ├─ lib/            # API helpers, auth utils
│  ├─ styles/         # Tailwind config, global.css
│  └─ types/          # TS interfaces
├─ .env.local
├─ next.config.js
├─ tailwind.config.js
├─ postcss.config.js
└─ package.json
```

---

## 4️⃣ Core Features & Sample Code

### 4.1 Navigation Bar

```tsx
// src/components/layout/Header.tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import { useSelector } from 'react-redux';
import { selectCartCount } from '@/store/cartSlice';

export default function Header() {
  const count = useSelector(selectCartCount);
  return (
    <header className="bg-white shadow-md">
      <nav className="container mx-auto flex justify-between items-center py-4">
        <Link href="/" passHref>
          <a className="text-xl font-bold">ShopLogo</a>
        </Link>
        <ul className="flex space-x-6">
          <li><Link href="/shop">Shop</Link></li>
          <li><Link href="/about">About</Link></li>
          <li><Link href="/contact">Contact</Link></li>
          <li>
            <Link href="/cart">
              <a className="relative">
                Cart
                {count > 0 && (
                  <span className="absolute -top-2 -right-2 bg-red-500 text-xs rounded-full w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center">
                    {count}
                  </span>
                )}
              </a>
            </Link>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </header>
  );
}
```

### 4.2 Product Card

```tsx
// src/components/pages/ProductCard.tsx
import Image from 'next/image';
import Link from 'next/link';
import { useDispatch } from 'react-redux';
import { addToCart } from '@/store/cartSlice';

export default function ProductCard({ product }) {
  const dispatch = useDispatch();

  return (
    <article className="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">
      <Link href={`/product/${product.slug}`} passHref>
        <a>
          <Image
            src={product.image}
            alt={product.title}
            width={300}
            height={300}
            className="object-cover"
          />
        </a>
      </Link>
      <div className="p-4">
        <h3 className="font-semibold">{product.title}</h3>
        <p className="text-gray-600">${product.price}</p>
        <button
          onClick={() => dispatch(addToCart(product))}
          className="mt-2 bg-indigo-600 text-white px-4 py-1 rounded hover:bg-indigo-700"
        >
          Add to Cart
        </button>
      </div>
    </article>
  );
}
```

### 4.3 Shopping Cart Page

```tsx
// src/pages/cart.tsx
import { useSelector, useDispatch } from 'react-redux';
import { selectCartItems, removeFromCart, clearCart } from '@/store/cartSlice';
import Link from 'next/link';

export default function CartPage() {
  const items = useSelector(selectCartItems);
  const dispatch = useDispatch();

  const total = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price * item.quantity, 0);

  return (
    <main className="container mx-auto py-8">
      <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Your Cart</h1>
      {items.length === 0 ? (
        <p>Your cart is empty. <Link href="/shop">Continue shopping</Link></p>
      ) : (
        <>
          <ul className="space-y-4">
            {items.map(item => (
              <li key={item.id} className="flex items-center justify-between">
                <div className="flex items-center space-x-4">
                  <img src={item.image} alt={item.title} className="w-16 h-16 object-cover" />
                  <div>
                    <h3>{item.title}</h3>
                    <p>${item.price} × {item.quantity}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <button onClick={() => dispatch(removeFromCart(item.id))}>Remove</button>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <div className="mt-6 flex justify-between items-center">
            <span className="font-semibold text-xl">Total: ${total.toFixed(2)}</span>
            <div>
              <button onClick={() => dispatch(clearCart())} className="mr-4">Clear Cart</button>
              <Link href="/checkout"><a className="bg-green-600 text-white px-6 py-2 rounded">Checkout</a></Link>
            </div>
          </div>
        </>
      )}
    </main>
  );
}
```

### 4.4 Checkout Flow (simplified)

```tsx
// src/pages/checkout.tsx
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { useRouter } from 'next/router';
import { useDispatch } from 'react-redux';
import { clearCart } from '@/store/cartSlice';
import { createOrder } from '@/lib/api'; // wrapper around your backend

export default function Checkout() {
  const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors } } = useForm();
  const router = useRouter();
  const dispatch = useDispatch();

  const onSubmit = async data => {
    try {
      await createOrder(data); // POST /orders
      dispatch(clearCart());
      router.push('/thank-you');
    } catch (err) {
      console.error(err);
      alert('Something went wrong. Please try again.');
    }
  };

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className="max-w-xl mx-auto">
      <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Checkout</h1>
      {/* Billing & Shipping fields */}
      <input {...register('name', { required: true })} placeholder="Full Name" />
      {/* ... other fields ... */}
      <button type="submit" className="mt-4 bg-indigo-600 text-white px-6 py-2 rounded">
        Place Order
      </button>
    </form>
  );
}
```

